.TH zwclock "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zwclock \- dock widget: time of day
.SH SYNOPSIS
started by \fBzdock\fR (catalog line \fB@Time:/usr/hr/bin/zwclock\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zwclock -- dock widget: time of day
Started by zdock from an @ line of /usr/hr/etc/dock; not run by hand.
Shows the time (HH:MM) and the day in a cell of the dock bar.
.HE
.B zwclock
is a widget of the
.B zdock
bar: a small resident program the dock starts from an
.B @
line of its catalog, showing the time of day
.RB ( HH : MM )
with the weekday and day of the month beneath, in an icon-sized cell
at the right end of the bar.
It redraws once a second, so the display follows the clock (and the
dock's own repaints) immediately.
.PP
It draws inside the dock's own window under the dock's clipping, owns
no window of its own, and takes no input itself; a left click on the
cell is the dock's, and the shipped catalog wires it to the full
.B zclock
application (switch to it when it runs, launch it when it does not),
so the Clock icon need not sit on the bar.
It exits by itself when the dock goes away.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B zdock ,
.B zview ,
.B zclock ,
.B date
.SH NOTES
Not meant to be run from a shell: it needs the cell contract
.RB ( \-W )
that only
.B zdock
supplies, and exits at once without it.
For a clock in a window of its own, see
.BR zclock .
